<title>JAPAN: Samsung to merge Japan units for listing - paper.</title>
<headline>Samsung to merge Japan units for listing - paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Group will merge its electronics and trading house units in Japan by the end of the year and aims to list shares of the merged firm on the Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) in 2001, a Japanese business daily reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun said the industrial group planned the listing on the second section of the TSE to raise funds and recruit workers.</p>
<p>The two units are Samsung Electronics Japan Co and Samsung Japan Co, the paper said. Officials of the firms were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
